# Mwinbarka Imports — project context

## What this project is

A lead-generation website for **Mwinbarka Imports**, an importation agent based in Ghana who
sources and imports goods from **China and Turkey** on behalf of customers.

This is NOT an e-commerce shop. There is no product catalog, no cart, and no online checkout.
The site's only job is to:

1. Explain what Mwinbarka Imports does and build trust
2. Get visitors to submit an "import request" describing what they want sourced
3. Route that request to the official chat line (and save it to a database) so the client can follow up
   and negotiate price/timeline manually

## Business model (important — do not build catalog/cart features)

- Customer submits a request (free text: "what do you want imported")
- Request is saved to Supabase AND auto-opens the official chat with a prefilled message
- All pricing, payment, and order confirmation happens off-site on the official line between
  the client and the customer
- There is NO payment gateway integration (no Paystack, no cards, no Mobile Money on-site)
- There is NO product listing/browsing — only example category images to inspire visitors

## Brand

- Business name: **Mwinbarka Imports**
- Logo: navy blue + gold globe/plane/box mark with wordmark (`assets/logo.png`)
- Colors:
  - Primary (Navy): `#0A1F44` (headers, nav, body text on light backgrounds)
  - Accent (Gold): `#C9A227` (buttons, CTAs, prices, highlights, icons)
  - Base: `#FFFFFF` / off-white (backgrounds)
- Tone: premium, trustworthy, professional — this is an agent asking people to trust them
  with money before goods arrive, so design should feel credible, not cheap or "market stall"

## Currency

- ALL prices, budgets, and monetary references on this site MUST be in **Ghana Cedis (GH₵)**.
- Never default to USD or generic "$" symbols.

## Target audience

- Ghanaian customers (mobile-first — most visitors will be on phones)
- The official line is the primary communication channel — say the word “WhatsApp” only once
  on the public site (Contact page). Everywhere else use “official line”, “chat”, or the number.
- Never show the word “1688” on the public site. Say “wholesale link”, “factory listing”, or “Alibaba”.

## Tech stack

- Frontend: plain HTML/CSS/JS, mobile-first, no build step
- Backend/Database: Supabase (`requests`, `profiles`, customer login/signup, staff admin — see `supabase/schema.sql`)
- Hosting/Deploy: Netlify (`netlify.toml`, publish from repo root)
- WhatsApp integration: `wa.me/233540309637?text=...` links, prefilled with form data
  (WhatsApp number: 0540309637 → international format 233540309637)

## Design/UX principles

- Mobile-first — most Ghanaian visitors will be on phones, design for small screens first
- Every page should have a clear path to either the official line or the request form — avoid dead ends
- Keep the request form short and low-friction (name, phone, what they want — rest optional)
  since the goal is capturing the lead, not collecting every detail upfront
- Use the gold accent sparingly and deliberately (CTAs, prices, key highlights) against navy/white
  rather than covering large areas — keep it feeling premium, not gaudy

## What NOT to build (explicitly out of scope for MVP)

- Shopping cart
- Product catalog with individual product pages
- Online payment/checkout (Paystack, cards, Mobile Money integration)
- Customer wallets, balances, or batch payment
- Order tracking beyond the customer’s own saved requests
